  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="484540d8-d62f-5024-96a5-82406ea48cf3" activityNameId="375864f2-b810-5a39-a623-47683a07deb6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Disposal, catalyst for EDC production, 0% water, to hazardous waste incineration</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Disposal, catalyst for EDC production, 0% water, to hazardous waste incineration
Inventoried waste contains 100% EDC Oxychlor catalyst; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 504000; H n.a.; C n.a.; S n.a.; N n.a.; P n.a.; B n.a.; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba n.a.; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr n.a.; Cu 55000; Hg n.a.; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb n.a.; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn n.a.; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 441000; Fe n.a.; Ca n.a.; Al n.a.; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. Net energy produced in HWI: 17.11MJ/kg electric energy and 1.27MJ/kg thermal energy Allocation of energy production: no substitution or expansion. 100% of burden allocated to waste disposal function of HWI. One kg of this waste produces 1.007 kg of residues, which are landfilled. Additional solidification with 0.4028 kg of cement.;; UUID: a272f922-90e7-44aa-a836-823629dd3229
waste-specific air and water emissions from incineration, auxiliary material consumption for flue gas cleaning. Short-term emissions to river water and long-term emissions to ground water from residual material landfill (from solidified fly ashes and scrubber slugde). Process energy demands for HWI.
Location: Specific to the technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Well applicable to modern incineration practices in Europe or North America or Japan.
Technology: Swiss HWI plant in 2000 with wet flue gas scrubber and low-dust SCR DeNOx facility. Gross thermal efficiency 74.4% and gross electric efficiency 10%.
Time period: Transfer coefficients for modern Swiss MSWI. Emission speciation based on early 90ies data.
Production volume: 2 Swiss HWI plants with a total capacity of 53'000 t/a.
Sampling: The 2 Swiss HWI plants, used as the inventory reference technology mix, have a total annual capacity of 53'000 tons of hazardous waste. This corresponds to 39% of the Swiss total installed capacity in 2000. Swiss average plants size is 20'000 t/a. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a272f922-90e7-44aa-a836-823629dd3229.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
